of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-greedy-survival"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-greedy-survival"],"id":"long.thm-greedy-survival","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 1.11 (Membership equals greedy survival; the fatal-gap dichotomy)","locator":"Long record Theorem 1.11, p. 24, label thm:greedy-survival","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For a real target $x\\ge0$, let $r_n(x)$ be the remainder after the greedy rule has processed weights $w_1,\\ldots,w_n$, and let $R_n=\\sum_{j>n}w_j$, with $r_0(x)=x$ and $R_0=E$. Then\n$$\nx\\in\\mathcal A\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n x\\ge0\\ \\text{ and }\\ r_n(x)\\le R_n\\ \\text{for every }n\\ge0.\n$$\nFor every $x\\in[0,E]$, nonmembership is equivalent to a finite strict gap between the two next-prefix intervals; see Observation 9.44.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-greedy-survival","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-greedy-survival","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-greedy-survival%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.paper_greedy_survival%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-greedy-survival%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.paper_greedy_survival%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.paper_greedy_survival"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-greedy-